Description: hw/rtc: Add the i.MX21 real-time clock
 The i.MX1/21/27 RTC keeps a 16-bit day counter and the hour, minute
 and second of the day, with an alarm on all four, a minute stopwatch,
 and interrupts every day, hour, minute, second and half second and at
 4 to 512 Hz. Linux's rtc-mxc drives it as fsl,imx21-rtc; the Chumby
 Classic's own 2.6.16 kernel has no driver for it.
 .
 Model the count on QEMU's RTC clock, starting from -rtc base= and
 counting days since 1970 as rtc-mxc does, so that the guest reads the
 host's date by default. Status flags are latched lazily from the count
 on every access, and a timer runs only for the next enabled event.
 Setting the time sends RTC_CHANGE. Disabling the RTC freezes the count;
 a software reset clears it. The block is in its own power domain, so a
 system reset leaves it running.
